.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.bak*
*.log

# secrets + generated state + data lake: never in history (the journal is data/, not git)
data/*
!data/nav_attestation.jsonl
!data/decision_ledger.json
!data/cashcarry_config.json
# The authority declaration is POLICY, not generated state: it says which component
# may reach which surface. It must be reviewable in a diff, because a grant that
# widens silently is the failure libs/ops/agent_authority.py exists to prevent.
!data/agent_authority.json
# The GPT-seat intelligence LEDGERS are institutional memory, not generated state: they record
# what was fetched, at what completeness, and what remains unread. Ungitted they die with the
# container, and the next session re-reads a corpus it has already paid for.
# Only the INPUT ledgers: external_intel.json is the generated report and stays out.
!data/intelligence/
!data/intelligence/video_channel_coverage.json
!data/intelligence/extreme_return_claims.json
!data/intelligence/practitioner_corpus.json
web/*
!web/index.html
reports/
lake/
docs/EXTERNAL_PANEL_DOSSIER.md
*.exe
tools/*.exe

# one-shot gate-optimality diagnostic scratch (6MB pickle + root-level probes)
_audit_prepared.pkl

# Coverage reports are MEASUREMENTS, not records. The ratcheted high-water marks live in
# docs/research/COVERAGE_RATCHET.json and are committed; the raw report is regenerated on every
# run and would otherwise churn a large file on every commit.
coverage.json
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Test-planted probes. `test_the_dead_caller_check_can_still_SEE_a_dead_caller` writes these into
# the tree and removes them in a `finally`, but a `git add -A` landing inside that window commits
# them -- which happened on 2026-08-08 and shipped two junk files to the branch. The test itself
# ASSERTS they are absent when it starts, so a leaked pair turns the suite red on the next run.
# Ignoring them makes the race harmless without weakening the test.
libs/_deadlink_probe.py
scripts/_deadlink_probe_caller.py
